    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "A structurally related heteroaryl amide PET radioligand showed moderate brain uptake in humans, providing translational evidence that this compound class has meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "A fluorophenyl benzoyl piperidine analogue showed sufficient brain uptake in rat micro-PET studies, supporting the CNS permeability of the aryl ketone/amide core shared with the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "PET studies indicate that the benzoyl-piperidine family is freely permeable across the blood-brain barrier, supporting the CNS access of the query's benzoyl-azetidine/piperazine framework.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple high-transferability experimental records from PET, biodistribution, and brain/plasma studies consistently show robust BBB penetration for structurally analogous aryl amide, indole, piperazine, and piperidine compounds. The query shares key CNS-permeable features with these validated scaffolds, supporting a pass prediction for meaningful CNS access.",
